==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kwæk/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-quack.ogg|Audio (GA)}}
* {{rhymes|en|æk|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|*quacken}}, {{m|enm|queken|t=to croak like a frog; make a noise like a duck, goose, or quail}}, from {{m|enm|quack}}, {{m|enm|qwacke}}, {{m|enm|quek}}, {{m|enm|queke|t=quack|pos=interjection and noun}}, also {{m|enm|kek}}, {{m|enm|keke}}, {{m|enm|whec-}}, partly of imitative origin and partly from {{der|en|dum|quacken|t=to croak, quack}}, from {{der|en|odt|*kwaken|t=to croak, quack}}, from {{der|en|gmw-pro|*kwakōn}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*kwakaną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*kwakōną|t=to croak}}, of imitative origin.<ref>Robert E. Lewis, ''Middle English dictionary, Volume 8'', queke.</ref> Cognate with {{cog|stq|kwoakje}}, {{m|stq|kwaakje|t=to quack}}, {{cog|gml|quaken|t=to quack, croak}}, {{cog|de|quaken|t=to quack, croak}}, {{cog|da|kvække|t=to croak}}, {{cog|sv|kväka|t=to croak, quackle}}, {{cog|no|kvekke|t=to croak}}, {{cog|is|kvaka|t=to twitter, chirp, quack}}.

